{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_xxqsqzbmfkzc7b7lvrjae72liadqszqyy25wnyrszjjqxkuqh62a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. All four phases done; the completion gate holds.\n\n## What the library is\n`c_src/src/lib.c` is a self-contained `stb_ds.h` implementation (dynamic array, open-addressing hash map with bucketed probing, siphash-2-4, string arena) plus the `hm_geti`/`strkey` test helpers. `include/lib.h` declares only `hm_geti`, but the `.so` exports 16 symbols.\n\n## Phase A — surface map\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — 16/16 C symbols exported by the Rust `.so` with exact names; **symbol diff empty**; 0 undefined non-libc imports (`ldd` → `libc`/`libgcc` only). No stubs were needed — no C module had been skipped. Also documents that `extern void stbds_unit_tests(void)` is declared but never defined, so it is correctly *not* a symbol of either `.so`.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 60 rows, mechanically grepped from every `return`/`assert`/null-check/threshold in the C.\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 73 rows over the axes the C actually branches on (`mode` ≤0/==1/≥2, `string.mode` 0–3 + out-of-range, 10 `elemsize`/`keysize` shapes, every rehash/shrink/tombstone boundary, all `len % 8` residues, arena block ladder…).\n- Feature combos: `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`**, so the valid set is `{default, --no-default-features}` — both `cargo check` clean.\n\n## Phases B–D — results\n86 tests per configuration, all through `libloading` on **both** `.so`s (never calling Rust directly). `check_all_configs.sh`: **516/516 passing across 2 feature configs × 2 profiles + cross-profile check**, symbol parity 16/16 each time.\n\n## Real divergences found and fixed\n1. **`SIGABRT` vs C's `SIGSEGV` on every null-pointer argument** (7 error rows). Cause: rustc's debug-assertion null-pointer-dereference checks, on by default in `dev` but off in `release` — the same source shipped two artifacts with different behaviour. Fixed with `[profile.dev] debug-assertions = false, overflow-checks = false`.\n2. **`cargo test` does not rebuild a `cdylib`-only lib target**, so the `.so` under test was silently stale. Found by mutation testing (first run: 0/16 caught). The harness now refuses to run on a stale artifact.\n\n## Skeptical checks beyond \"tests pass\"\n- **`mutation_check.sh`**: 33 injected deviations → **30 killed, 0 real gaps**. The 3 survivors are *proven* equivalent mutants (the `hash < 2` fixup needs a 64-bit hash of exactly 0/1 — `p = 2⁻⁶³`, 0 of 400 000 observed; `min_cap <= 2*cap` whose body is a no-op). Two gaps the mutations exposed were closed with new tests (row 70/70b high-load tombstone rebuild for the quadratic re-probe; `e13b` arena release).\n- Non-state behaviour needed non-state probes: leaks (`ERRORS.md` 13b/38 — the \"free the strdup'd key only when `mode == 1` exactly\" quirk) are detected via a glibc tcache-LIFO `malloc` probe; `storage` alignment and both `realloc` sizes via `STBDS_ALIGN_FWD`/`malloc_usable_size` assertions.\n- `stbds_hash_index::temp_key` is **never initialised** by `stbds_make_hash_index` — excluded from snapshots and compared only where C defines it.\n- `stbds_stralloc` is additionally checked against an independent oracle model, which pins the oversize-block splice position and the masked-shift block ladder.\n\n6 `ERRORS.md` rows carry no test: they are asserts on internal invariants of `static` helpers (`slot_count == 0`, `i+1 <= arrcap`, `slot < slot_count`, …) with no reachable trigger through any exported symbol, plus the vacuous `assert(used_count >= 0)` on a `size_t` — for that one `e37` forces the wrap to `SIZE_MAX` and proves Rust does *not* turn it into a real check. Each is documented with its reasoning rather than papered over with a fake test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3160,"cache_read_input_tokens":342005,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3160,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ffc982f6-75d4-4e7e-8887-c73d5a1dc23f","uuid":"f50900ef-f4ab-407d-8233-4b59e1317b93","timestamp":"2026-08-20T10:59:17.600Z"}
